W365 CLOUD PC UNDER REVIEW

Placing a Cloud PC under review refers to the process of taking a snapshot of the Cloud PC for security and investigation purposes. You may have to place a Cloud PC under review for any of these scenarios:
•	A request from an internal Security Operation Center (SOC) team
•	A response to a request from an internal or external third-party auditor
•	As a response to a pending or ongoing legal investigation
Up to 10 Cloud PCs can be placed under review simultaneously. If more than 10 are placed under review at once, the requests are queued, but the possibility of timeouts increases if they remain too long in the queue. To avoid timeouts, it is recommended to stagger the requests to allow sufficient time for previous requests to complete first.

Requirements
To place a Cloud PC under review, you need:
•	A Windows 365 Enterprise license
•	An Azure Storage account in the same tenant, set up according to the specified requirements


